    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive engine. His score of 80.98 is the only entry in our \"Strong\" tier, driven by a high-leverage leadoff spot against R. L\u00f3pez and a robust 0.371 xwOBA. **Lars Nootbaar** also earns a recommendation with a 65.16 score, largely thanks to a significant platoon advantage and the premium value provided by his leadoff status against S. Alcantara. While **Carson Benge** (61.14) cracks the 60-point threshold to secure a start, the remainder of the lineup relies on marginal utility; **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** provide stable, albeit unspectacular, production in the middle of the order despite the standard R/R platoon suppression.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Chase Meidroth**, who fell just short of our 40-point floor with a 33.18 efficiency score. Despite his potential, the matchup against G. Williams\u2014who possesses a stifling 2.89 xERA\u2014severely hampered his outlook, with the optimizer penalizing him 19% for the high level of opposing skill. With **Trea Turner**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Christian Yelich** all unavailable due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is severely restricted. We are particularly cautious regarding the output from **Dillon Dingler** (43.73) and **Josh Smith** (53.59); both are currently active only because we are maximizing our game caps, but their negative platoon adjustments suggest a high likelihood of early-inning stagnation. Monitor the stadium conditions for **Dillon Dingler** specifically, as any drop in wind-aided output could push his performance into the sub-40 range, warranting a close watch on his defensive utility throughout the contest.",
